<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs and Detailed Derivations</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Counting function and effective dimension</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Counting function and effective dimension)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(t):=\#\{i\geq 1:\lambda_{i}\geq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(t):=\#\{i\geq 1:\lambda_{i}\geq t\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Assumption R (Spectral redundancy / tail). ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)=\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\;\asymp\;\lambda^{-1/\beta}\qquad(\lambda\downarrow 0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≍</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)=\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\;\asymp\;\lambda^{-1/\beta}\qquad(\lambda\downarrow 0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph">Proof.</em><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
From <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{i}\asymp i^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≍</mo><mi>i</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\asymp i^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the largest <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\geq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\geq t</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfies <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\asymp t^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≍</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\asymp t^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I_{\lambda}:=\max\{i\geq 1:\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda\}\asymp\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\lambda}:=\max\{i\geq 1:\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda\}\asymp\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Split
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)=\sum_{i=1}^{I_{\lambda}}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}+\sum_{i=I_{\lambda}+1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)=\sum_{i=1}^{I_{\lambda}}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}+\sum_{i=I_{\lambda}+1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq I_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq I_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> so
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\geq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\geq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence the head sum
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\gtrsim I_{\lambda}\asymp\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≳</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>≍</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gtrsim I_{\lambda}\asymp\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;I_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;I_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&lt;\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&lt;\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\leq\lambda_{i}/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\leq\lambda_{i}/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the tail sum <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\leq\lambda^{-1}\sum_{i=I_{\lambda}+1}^{\infty}\lambda_{i}\lesssim\lambda^{-1}\int_{I_{\lambda}}^{\infty}x^{-1/\beta}\,dx\asymp\lambda^{-1}I_{\lambda}^{1-1/\beta}\asymp\lambda^{-1}(\lambda^{-1/\beta})^{1-1/\beta}=\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\lambda^{-1}\sum_{i=I_{\lambda}+1}^{\infty}\lambda_{i}\lesssim\lambda^{-1}\int_{I_{\lambda}}^{\infty}x^{-1/\beta}\,dx\asymp\lambda^{-1}I_{\lambda}^{1-1/\beta}\asymp\lambda^{-1}(\lambda^{-1/\beta})^{1-1/\beta}=\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, lower bounds can be derived using the constants <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{-},c_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{-},c_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding matching asymptotics up to constants. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Bias bound from the source condition</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bias bound from the source condition)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\lambda,\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\lambda,\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> be the population ridge solution
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\|f_{\lambda,\infty}-f^{*}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}}_{\text{bias}^{2}}\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\Big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\Big)^{2}\langle f^{*},u_{i}\rangle^{2}\;\leq\;\lambda^{2s}\,C_{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bias</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\|f_{\lambda,\infty}-f^{*}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}}_{\text{bias}^{2}}\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\Big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\Big)^{2}\langle f^{*},u_{i}\rangle^{2}\;\leq\;\lambda^{2s}\,C_{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph">Proof.</em><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Using (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In Assumption S (Source condition / target smoothness). ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), the <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th coefficient equals
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\big)^{2}\lambda_{i}^{2s}\langle g,u_{i}\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\big)^{2}\lambda_{i}^{2s}\langle g,u_{i}\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\leq\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\leq\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> (with the latter <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, but more precisely, <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\big)\lambda_{i}^{s}\leq\lambda^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\big)\lambda_{i}^{s}\leq\lambda^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> by direct inequality: if <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\geq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, the ratio <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1\leq(\lambda_{i}/\lambda)^{-s}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1\leq(\lambda_{i}/\lambda)^{-s}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&lt;\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&lt;\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\lambda_{i}^{s}&lt;\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}}\lambda_{i}^{s}=\lambda\lambda_{i}^{s-1}&lt;\lambda^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\lambda_{i}^{s}&lt;\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}}\lambda_{i}^{s}=\lambda\lambda_{i}^{s-1}&lt;\lambda^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s-1\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s-1\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&lt;\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&lt;\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus,
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\big)^{2}\lambda_{i}^{2s}\leq\lambda^{2s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}\big)^{2}\lambda_{i}^{2s}\leq\lambda^{2s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Summing over <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> yields the claim, as the series converges by the bound on <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Variance bound via effective dimension</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance bound via effective dimension)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\lambda,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\lambda,n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the empirical ridge estimator with i.i.d. zero-mean
noise of variance <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,\|f_{\lambda,n}-f_{\lambda,\infty}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}\;\leq\;C\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,\|f_{\lambda,n}-f_{\lambda,\infty}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}\;\leq\;C\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for an absolute constant <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}(f_{\lambda,n})}_{\text{excess risk}}\;\leq\;C_{1}\,\lambda^{2s}\;+\;C_{2}\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">excess risk</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}(f_{\lambda,n})}_{\text{excess risk}}\;\leq\;C_{1}\,\lambda^{2s}\;+\;C_{2}\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><em id="Thmlemma3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph">Proof.</em><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
The variance bound follows from standard operator concentration for kernel ridge regression under i.i.d. samples. Specifically, projecting onto the eigenbasis <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(u_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(u_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the estimator’s <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th coordinate variance is at most <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma^{2}/n)\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}+\lambda)^{2}}\leq(\sigma^{2}/n)\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma^{2}/n)\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}+\lambda)^{2}}\leq(\sigma^{2}/n)\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\lambda_{i}+\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma^{2}/n)N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma^{2}/n)N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. The operator form uses the Hilbert-Schmidt norm: <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1/2}(\hat{T}_{K}-T_{K})(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}\leq C(\sigma^{2}/n)\operatorname{Tr}[T_{K}(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}]=C(\sigma^{2}/n)N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>HS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1/2}(\hat{T}_{K}-T_{K})(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}\leq C(\sigma^{2}/n)\operatorname{Tr}[T_{K}(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}]=C(\sigma^{2}/n)N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{T}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{T}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical covariance. The excess risk bound combines this with the bias term. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Scaling law with redundancy-controlled exponent). ‣ Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Scaling law with redundancy-controlled exponent). ‣ Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</em>
The derivative is <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi^{\prime}(\lambda)=2sA\lambda^{2s-1}-\frac{1}{\beta}B(\sigma^{2}/n)\lambda^{-1/\beta-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}(\lambda)=2sA\lambda^{2s-1}-\frac{1}{\beta}B(\sigma^{2}/n)\lambda^{-1/\beta-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Setting <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}(\lambda^{\star})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}(\lambda^{\star})=0</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2sA(\lambda^{\star})^{2s-1}=\frac{1}{\beta}B(\sigma^{2}/n)(\lambda^{\star})^{-1/\beta-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sA(\lambda^{\star})^{2s-1}=\frac{1}{\beta}B(\sigma^{2}/n)(\lambda^{\star})^{-1/\beta-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda^{\star})^{2s+1/\beta}=\frac{1}{2s}\frac{B}{A}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\frac{1}{1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda^{\star})^{2s+1/\beta}=\frac{1}{2s}\frac{B}{A}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\frac{1}{1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda^{\star}\asymp n^{-1/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≍</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}\asymp n^{-1/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substitution into the bound gives <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda^{2s}\asymp n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≍</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{2s}\asymp n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\lambda^{-1/\beta}\asymp n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≍</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\lambda^{-1/\beta}\asymp n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>, matching up to constants. Strict convexity holds since <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi^{\prime\prime}(\lambda)=2s(2s-1)A\lambda^{2s-2}+\frac{1}{\beta}(\frac{1}{\beta}+1)B(\sigma^{2}/n)\lambda^{-1/\beta-2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime\prime}(\lambda)=2s(2s-1)A\lambda^{2s-2}+\frac{1}{\beta}(\frac{1}{\beta}+1)B(\sigma^{2}/n)\lambda^{-1/\beta-2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Representation invariance). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Representation invariance). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</em>
By the min–max (Courant–Fischer) theorem for self-adjoint operators and the frame bounds on <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{2}\langle T_{K}v,v\rangle\leq\langle T^{\prime}v,v\rangle\leq M^{2}\langle T_{K}v,v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{2}\langle T_{K}v,v\rangle\leq\langle T^{\prime}v,v\rangle\leq M^{2}\langle T_{K}v,v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, the spectra interlace up to scaling: there exist <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{-},c_{+}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{-},c_{+}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (depending on <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,M</annotation></semantics></math>) such that
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{-}\lambda_{i}(T_{K})\leq\lambda_{i}(T^{\prime})\leq c_{+}\lambda_{i}(T_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{-}\lambda_{i}(T_{K})\leq\lambda_{i}(T^{\prime})\leq c_{+}\lambda_{i}(T_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This preserves the regular variation of the tail (polynomial decay rate <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>), thus the counting function
order <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{T^{\prime}}(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{T^{\prime}}(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\prime}_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\prime}_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> asymptotic follows by monotonicity of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto x/(x+\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto x/(x+\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and comparison with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. The exponent <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, hence invariant. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Mixtures of domains). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Mixtures of domains). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</em>
For the counting function, by Weyl’s inequalities for sums of positive operators,
<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{T}(t)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{K}N_{T_{k}}(t/w_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{T}(t)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{K}N_{T_{k}}(t/w_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{T}(t)\geq\max_{k=1}^{K}N_{T_{k}}(t/c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{T}(t)\geq\max_{k=1}^{K}N_{T_{k}}(t/c)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{T_{k}}(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{T_{k}}(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the slowest decay (largest <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
i.e. smallest <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) dominates both bounds, yielding <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{T}(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{T}(t)\asymp t^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\min_{k}\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\min_{k}\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> asymptotic and the exponent <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> follow from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Counting function and effective dimension). ‣ A.1 Counting function and effective dimension ‣ Appendix A Proofs and Detailed Derivations ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="proposition 1 (Redundancy reduction improves 𝛼). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="proposition 1 (Redundancy reduction improves 𝛼). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</em>
The assumption implies <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{\widetilde{T}}(t)\lesssim t^{-1/\beta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\widetilde{T}}(t)\lesssim t^{-1/\beta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for small <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, by a similar counting argument as in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Counting function and effective dimension). ‣ A.1 Counting function and effective dimension ‣ Appendix A Proofs and Detailed Derivations ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Hence,
<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\widetilde{T}}(\lambda)\lesssim\lambda^{-1/\beta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\widetilde{T}}(\lambda)\lesssim\lambda^{-1/\beta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (upper bound matching the asymptotic). The bias–variance optimization proceeds as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Scaling law with redundancy-controlled exponent). ‣ Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> replacing <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,
yielding the stated monotonicity of <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in the tail index, since <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\alpha/\partial\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\alpha/\partial\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Variance bound under mixing</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance bound under mixing)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the above mixing and moment conditions, the kernel ridge variance satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,\|f_{\lambda,n}-f_{\lambda,\infty}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}\;\leq\;C\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n_{\mathrm{eff}}}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,\|f_{\lambda,n}-f_{\lambda,\infty}\|_{L^{2}}^{2}\;\leq\;C\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n_{\mathrm{eff}}}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for a constant <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> depending only on the mixing profile and moments.
Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}(f_{\lambda,n})\;\leq\;C_{1}\,\lambda^{2s}+C_{2}\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n_{\mathrm{eff}}}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}(f_{\lambda,n})\;\leq\;C_{1}\,\lambda^{2s}+C_{2}\,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n_{\mathrm{eff}}}\,N_{\mathrm{eff}}(\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><em id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph">Proof.</em><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
By projecting onto the eigenbasis and employing a standard blocking argument for <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-mixing sequences (dividing into near-independent blocks of size depending on mixing decay), the covariances of empirical coefficients are summable under the condition <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\beta(k)^{\gamma/(2+\gamma)}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\beta(k)^{\gamma/(2+\gamma)}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the factor <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{eff}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>eff</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{eff}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the variance bound. The operator form mirrors Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Variance bound via effective dimension). ‣ A.3 Variance bound via effective dimension ‣ Appendix A Proofs and Detailed Derivations ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, with covariance inflation bounded by the mixing coefficients. Detailed bounds can be found in standard references on mixing processes in kernel methods. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Scaling law with mixing). ‣ 2.1 Non-i.i.d. data: mixing and effective sample size ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Scaling law with mixing). ‣ 2.1 Non-i.i.d. data: mixing and effective sample size ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</em>
Replace <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) via Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (Variance bound under mixing). ‣ A.8 Variance bound under mixing ‣ Appendix A Proofs and Detailed Derivations ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>
and repeat the bias–variance optimization verbatim as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Scaling law with redundancy-controlled exponent). ‣ Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.10 </span>Tail index preservation under small perturbations</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Tail index preservation under small perturbations)<span id="Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> has tail index <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|T_{m}-T_{K}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq C_{0}m^{-r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|T_{m}-T_{K}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq C_{0}m^{-r}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then for all sufficiently large <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{-}\,i^{-1/\beta}\;\lesssim\;\lambda_{i}(T_{m})\;\lesssim\;c_{+}\,i^{-1/\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≲</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≲</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{-}\,i^{-1/\beta}\;\lesssim\;\lambda_{i}(T_{m})\;\lesssim\;c_{+}\,i^{-1/\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e. <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> shares the same tail index <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> up to constants.
<em id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Proof.</em>
By Weyl’s inequalities for self-adjoint compact operators, <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{i}(T_{m})-\lambda_{i}(T_{K})|\leq\|T_{m}-T_{K}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq C_{0}m^{-r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{i}(T_{m})-\lambda_{i}(T_{K})|\leq\|T_{m}-T_{K}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq C_{0}m^{-r}</annotation></semantics></math>. For large <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}(T_{K})\gg C_{0}m^{-r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}(T_{K})\gg C_{0}m^{-r}</annotation></semantics></math>, the perturbation is subdominant, preserving the asymptotic order <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{i}(T_{m})\asymp i^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}(T_{m})\asymp i^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> (regular variation of polynomial tails ensures stability under <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(\lambda_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(\lambda_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations). ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.11 </span>Bias–variance with RF width</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bias–variance with RF width)<span id="Thmlemma6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For ridge on <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples and width <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}(f_{\lambda,n}^{(m)})\;\leq\;C_{1}\lambda^{2s}\;+\;C_{2}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)\;+\;C_{3}\,\mathfrak{R}(m,\lambda)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}(f_{\lambda,n}^{(m)})\;\leq\;C_{1}\lambda^{2s}\;+\;C_{2}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)\;+\;C_{3}\,\mathfrak{R}(m,\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)=\mathrm{Tr}\!\big((T_{m}+\lambda I)^{-1}T_{m}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.032em;" width="1.032em"><mi>Tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)=\mathrm{Tr}\!\big((T_{m}+\lambda I)^{-1}T_{m}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(m,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(m,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is the RF approximation term satisfying
<math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(m,\lambda)\leq C_{4}m^{-r}\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(m,\lambda)\leq C_{4}m^{-r}\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> under the
spectral-approximation assumption.
<em id="Thmlemma6.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Proof.</em>
Decompose the error as <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\lambda,n}^{(m)}-f^{*}=(f_{\lambda,n}^{(m)}-f_{\lambda,\infty}^{(m)})+(f_{\lambda,\infty}^{(m)}-f_{\lambda,\infty})+(f_{\lambda,\infty}-f^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\lambda,n}^{(m)}-f^{*}=(f_{\lambda,n}^{(m)}-f_{\lambda,\infty}^{(m)})+(f_{\lambda,\infty}^{(m)}-f_{\lambda,\infty})+(f_{\lambda,\infty}-f^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. The first term is variance on <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}\leq C_{2}(\sigma^{2}/n)N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}\leq C_{2}(\sigma^{2}/n)N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>; the third is bias on <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}\leq C_{1}\lambda^{2s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}\leq C_{1}\lambda^{2s}</annotation></semantics></math>; the second is approximation error bounded by <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|T_{m}-T_{K}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|T_{m}-T_{K}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> times resolvent stability <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}\|\lesssim\lambda^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(T_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}\|\lesssim\lambda^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, refined to <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m^{-r}\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{-r}\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> via the trace difference in the assumption. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.12 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Scaling with finite width). ‣ Assumption (Spectral approximation). ‣ 2.2 Finite-width random features: spectral approximation ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Scaling with finite width). ‣ Assumption (Spectral approximation). ‣ 2.2 Finite-width random features: spectral approximation ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</em>
By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Tail index preservation under small perturbations). ‣ A.10 Tail index preservation under small perturbations ‣ Appendix A Proofs and Detailed Derivations ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same tail index <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)\asymp\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{(m)}(\lambda)\asymp\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6 (Bias–variance with RF width). ‣ A.11 Bias–variance with RF width ‣ Appendix A Proofs and Detailed Derivations ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> yields
<math id="A1.SS12.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}\lesssim\lambda^{2s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\lambda^{-1/\beta}+m^{-r}\lambda^{-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>≲</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,\mathcal{E}\lesssim\lambda^{2s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\lambda^{-1/\beta}+m^{-r}\lambda^{-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. At the optimum <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda^{\star}\asymp n^{-1/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≍</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}\asymp n^{-1/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sample variance term is <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\gtrsim n^{r/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\gtrsim n^{r/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures the RF term <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lesssim n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lesssim n^{-2s/(2s+1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>, subdominant. Thus, optimization as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Scaling law with redundancy-controlled exponent). ‣ Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> yields the claimed asymptotic. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.13 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Transformer scaling in the linearized regime). ‣ Assumption T2 (Implicit regularization ≈ ridge). ‣ 3.1 Linearized Transformers: NTK / random-features regime ‣ 3 Transformers: from kernels to deep nonlinearity ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Transformer scaling in the linearized regime). ‣ Assumption T2 (Implicit regularization ≈ ridge). ‣ 3.1 Linearized Transformers: NTK / random-features regime ‣ 3 Transformers: from kernels to deep nonlinearity ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</em>
The bound follows identically to Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Scaling law with redundancy-controlled exponent). ‣ Estimator. ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> after replacing <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{tr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>tr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{tr}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The tail index <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\mathrm{tr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>tr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\mathrm{tr}}</annotation></semantics></math> is preserved by: (i) sum over layers and heads (by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Mixtures of domains). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, as a convex combination); (ii) LayerNorm/residual bi-Lipschitz reparametrization (by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Representation invariance). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, preserving asymptotic tail order). Early-stopped SGD equivalence to ridge provides the <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> parameterization. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS14" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.14 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7 (Transformer scaling with kernel drift). ‣ Assumption T3 (Adiabatic tail stability). ‣ 3.2 Beyond linearization: feature learning with adiabatic kernel drift ‣ 3 Transformers: from kernels to deep nonlinearity ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7 (Transformer scaling with kernel drift). ‣ Assumption T3 (Adiabatic tail stability). ‣ 3.2 Beyond linearization: feature learning with adiabatic kernel drift ‣ 3 Transformers: from kernels to deep nonlinearity ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</em>
Use operator triangle inequalities to bound the cumulative resolvent drift error: <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(\bar{T}+\lambda I)^{-1}-(T_{1}+\lambda I)^{-1}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\sum_{t}\Delta_{t}(\lambda)/T=O(1/T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(\bar{T}+\lambda I)^{-1}-(T_{1}+\lambda I)^{-1}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\sum_{t}\Delta_{t}(\lambda)/T=O(1/T)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is negligible for large <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. The effective dimension <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\bar{T}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>eff</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\bar{T}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is sandwiched between asymptotics from <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> by comparison inequalities. The bias term remains <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{2s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{2s}</annotation></semantics></math> by the source condition in the time-averaged RKHS (assuming <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the condition uniformly over <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>); optimizing <math id="A1.SS14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> gives the stated exponent interval. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS15" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.15 </span>Proof of Corollary (Scaling with context)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof of Corollary (Scaling with context).</em>
The proof follows from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Scaling law with mixing). ‣ 2.1 Non-i.i.d. data: mixing and effective sample size ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> applied to the sequence mixing assumption T4, preserving the exponent while adjusting constants via <math id="A1.SS15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For growing <math id="A1.SS15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, the kernel augmentation preserves the tail index by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Mixtures of domains). ‣ Universality: representation invariance and multi-domain mixtures ‣ 2 Main Result: Scaling Laws as Redundancy Laws ‣ Scaling Laws are Redundancy Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> if new components have steeper or equal tails. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
